{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8f3c1a52-0d47-4c1e-9b6a-2e7d5c4f1a90",
    "name": "Spring Security JWT Audit",
    "description": "A stateless REST API with rotating JWT refresh tokens, hierarchical roles, per-IP rate limiting and an audit trail.\n\n## Getting started\n\n1. `docker compose up -d` in the repository root.\n2. Import `postman/environment.demo.json` and select it.\n3. Run **Auth > Login (admin)**. It stores the access token, so every other request is authenticated with no copying by hand.\n\nThe refresh token is never handled manually: it arrives in an `HttpOnly` cookie and Postman's cookie jar sends it back.\n\n## Running the whole thing\n\nThe Collection Runner executes the folders in order and every request carries assertions, so a full run is a live check of the API rather than a click-through. Run **Rate limiting** last — it empties the login bucket on purpose.\n\n## Demo accounts\n\n`admin`, `manager` and `user`, all with password `Demo1234!`, seeded by a Flyway migration in every profile.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// A stable User-Agent matters here: a refresh token is bound to the",
          "// client that obtained it and is refused from any other."
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userAccessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "createdUserId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "createdUsername",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "newUsername",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "lastLoginFailure",
      "value": "",
